@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Project Integration
	Testing project sync updates in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENOSBA |
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen OSB Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View new portal project
	New Portal projects that are added to Zendesk via OSB sync should have the appropriate parameters and tags.

	Given I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Regular            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the tag "liferay_portal"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the tag "regular"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the tag "us"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the tag "gold"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the tag "english"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the tag "approved"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not have the tag "liferay_dxp"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not have the tag "platinum"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not have the tag "premier"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not have the tag "closed"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the following parameters
	| Name                       | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Details                    | 123 Main Street    |
	| Details                    | United States      |
	| Details                    | 123 Main Street    |
	| Details                    | California         |
	| SLA                        | Gold               |
	| Status                     | Approved           |
	| Support Region             | US                 |
	| Support Language           | English            |
	| Tier                       | Regular            |
	| Account Code               | ZENOSBA            |
	| Partner First Line Support | false              |
	And the support account ID of the project with the code "ZENOSBA" should match the organization external ID on zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View resynced portal project
	Portal projects that are resynced to Zendesk via OSB sync should have the appropriate parameters and tags.

	Given I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Regular            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I assign an organization "Zen OSB Automotive" with the following tags while replacing existing tags
	| liferay_dxp |
	| premier     |
 	| platinum    |
	| closed      |
	| japan       |
	| japanese    |
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I sync the project with the code "ZENOSBA" to zendesk
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the tag "liferay_portal"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the tag "regular"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the tag "us"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the tag "gold"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the tag "english"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the tag "approved"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not have the tag "liferay_dxp"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not have the tag "platinum"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not have the tag "premier"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not have the tag "closed"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not have the tag "japan"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not have the tag "japanese"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should have the following parameters
	| Name                       | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Details                    | 123 Main Street    |
	| Details                    | United States      |
	| Details                    | 123 Main Street    |
	| Details                    | California         |
	| SLA                        | Gold               |
	| Status                     | Approved           |
	| Support Region             | US                 |
	| Support Language           | English            |
	| Tier                       | Regular            |
	| Account Code               | ZENOSBA            |
	| Partner First Line Support | false              |
	And the support account ID of the project with the code "ZENOSBA" should match the organization external ID on zendesk.liferay.com

